    "title": "UK women advance to NCAA second round with win over James Madison",
    "text": "Tonie Morgan scored 18 points and added seven rebounds and seven assists as No. 5 seed Kentucky beat No. 12 seed James Madison 71-56 in an NCAA Tournament first round game on Saturday in Morgantown, West Virginia. The Cats jumped out to a 36-10 lead and led 43-18 at the half. Clara Strack added 10 points and 14 rebounds for the Cats. Amelia Hassett had 14 points and Teonni Key nine points and 10 rebounds. James Madison is the alma mater of UK head coach Kenny Brooks. He is in the Dukes Hall of Fame, played there and coached the women's team for 14 seasons, including six trips to the NCAA Tournament. The Cats (24-10) advance to a second round game in Morgantown on Monday against either No. 4 West VIrginia or No. 13 Miami University. Tonie Morgan scored 18 points and added seven rebounds and seven assists as No. 5 seed Kentucky beat No. 12 seed James Madison 71-56 in an NCAA Tournament first round game on Saturday in Morgantown, West Virginia. The Cats jumped out to a 36-10 lead and led 43-18 at the half. Clara Strack added 10 points and 14 rebounds for the Cats. Amelia Hassett had 14 points and Teonni Key nine points and 10 rebounds. James Madison is the alma mater of UK head coach Kenny Brooks. He is in the Dukes Hall of Fame, played there and coached the women's team for 14 seasons, including six trips to the NCAA Tournament. The Cats (24-10) advance to a second round game in Morgantown on Monday against either No. 4 West VIrginia or No. 13 Miami University.",
